   586	## 7. Candidate card
   587	
   588	- **Mechanism.** A Lehman/HH one-sided exponent collision. Weighted sums Bp + Aq are
   589	  locked mod M² on the N-determined classes Br² ≡ AN (mod M), for **many prime moduli**
   590	  M ≈ N^{1/6} and small fixed weights. One baby list γ^i (γ = β^{∏M²}) is shared by all
   591	  moduli through cofactor-powered handles.
   592	- **Representation.** (Z/N)^*. Targets (v, M, r). The design uses only N (Legendre data
   593	  mod small public primes).
   594	- **Factor feature.** g = (Bp + Aq − c)/M² in a whole-range window of size ≈ N^{1/6}.
   595	  **Extraction.** Product tree / Bluestein gcd (Alg. 4.1), or exact match plus Lemma 3.1.
   596	- **Outcome.**
   597	  - Model lower bound N^{1/6} (proved).
   598	  - DCL attains N^{1/6+o(1)} on average (proved, search model) and in the worst case under
   599	    DCH (conjectured).
   600	  - Experiments: slope 0.171 at 95% success; full coverage at λ ≈ ln√N exhaustively to 48
   601	    bits.
   602	- **Scoped obstruction.**
   603	  - Below N^{1/6}, nothing in the one-base sumset model works (Thm A).
   604	  - Below N^{1/5}, nothing works with N^{o(1)} moduli or with degree ≥ 2 targets
   605	    (Thms A′, B).
   606	- **What would escape / is missing.**
   607	  - A proof of DCH, or a structured choice of (v, M) with provable full coverage.
   608	  - An order lemma for β^L.
   609	  - A ratio-uniform version (§3.9).
   610	  - Going below 1/6 needs a non-sumset collision mechanism, and also faster small-factor
   611	    removal than Strassen.
   612	
