Take j₀ minimising v(T_j) for j ≤ K and use Δ^{j₀}f(0) = j₀! Σ_{n≥j₀} S(n,j₀)T_nℓ^{an}
∈ Z_ℓ. For a > c_W the n = j₀ term dominates, so v(T_{j₀}) ≥ −a j₀ − v(j₀!). Hence
v* ≥ −aK − v(K!) − c_W. If a ≤ c_W, pass to the subclass mod ℓ^{c_W+1}; the extra is
bounded. ∎

