The independent exact checks reproduce the coverage pattern. For the special 32-bit-scale instance, the \(\lambda\approx3\) design leaves 377 of 19,195 integer candidates uncovered (1.964%); the larger-\(\lambda\) design leaves none. Separately, my code exhaustively checked balanced prime pairs at 18, 22, and 26 bits, with no failures of the coverage equivalence or modulus-squared lock.

The literature comparison also needs a population caveat: “almost all semiprimes” without a balance condition is much weaker, since most such semiprimes have a small factor.
